  - line: 84
    type: narration
    text: "```"
  - line: 85
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 2: THE GUARDIAN AWAKENS"
  - line: 87
    type: narration
    text: "The final chamber took their breath away."
  - line: 89
    type: narration
    text: "It was a massive geodesic space, walls faceted with crystalline formations that refracted what little light they carried into impossible patterns."
  - line: 90
    type: narration
    text: "At the center, suspended in a beam of pure, gentle radiance, floated the Shard of First Dawn."
  - line: 92
    type: narration
    text: "It was beautiful."
  - line: 93
    type: narration
    text: "A tear of captured sunlight in a world that had never known such warmth."
  - line: 94
    type: narration
    text: "Its light didn't push back the darkness so much as coexist with it, illuminating without aggression."
  - line: 96
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"It's... peaceful,\""
  - line: 98
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Luminaire
    text: "\"It was never meant to be a weapon,\""
  - line: 100
    type: narration
    text: "As they approached, the chamber reacted."
  - line: 102
    type: narration
    text: "The crystalline formations around them began to vibrate, then crack."
  - line: 103
    type: narration
    text: "From the fractures seeped a sickly, tarnished light that coalesced into a humanoid form—tall, majestic, but twisted with corruption."
  - line: 104
    type: narration
    text: "Its features were blurred, as if viewed through warped glass, and its voice echoed with madness and hunger."
  - line: 106
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"MORE VESSELS. MORE LIGHT TO CONSUME.\""
  - line: 108
    type: narration
    text: "The Guardian didn't stand guard over the Shard."
  - line: 109
    type: narration
    text: "It was chained to it—tendrils of corrupted light connecting it to the radiant crystal, feeding on its purity even as it corrupted that same energy."
  - line: 111
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"It's not a guardian,\""
  - line: 112
    type: narration
    text: "Vek'tar realized, his chroniton sight showing him the truth. \"It's the prisoner. The thing the Vault was built to contain. It's been feeding on the Shard for centuries.\""
  - line: 114
    type: narration
    text: "The fight was brutal."
  - line: 115
    type: narration
    text: "The Guardian moved with impossible speed, striking from angles that defied geometry."
  - line: 116
    type: narration
    text: "It adapted to their patterns, learning and countering."
  - line: 117
    type: narration
    text: "Each time they wounded it, the tendrils connecting it to the Shard pulsed, and the injuries healed."
  - line: 119
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's cleaver shattered one of its arms, only to watch it reform in seconds."
  - line: 120
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's dragon armor deflected beams of corrupted light that would have unmade matter, but the feedback staggered him."
  - line: 122
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"It's drawing power from the Shard!\""
  - line: 124
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 3: VEK'TAR'S SACRIFICE"
  - line: 126
    type: narration
    text: "They were losing."
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "The Guardian was learning, growing stronger with each exchange."
  - line: 128
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck bled from a dozen shallow cuts that refused to clot."
  - line: 129
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's armor was spiderwebbed with cracks, glowing lines of strain."
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "Vek'tar watched, his chroniton sight showing him the timelines."
  - line: 132
    type: narration
    text: "Most ended in their deaths."
  - line: 133
    type: narration
    text: "But one—a fragile, branching path—showed a possibility."
  - line: 135
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"I can sever the connection,\""
  - line: 137
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt deflected another beam."
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "\"How?\""
  - line: 140
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Phase into the Shard itself. Disrupt the bond from the inside.\""
  - line: 142
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"Vek, no—\""
  - line: 144
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Raw Light energy will burn through my chroniton structure. I know. I'm at ninety-four percent decay anyway. Weeks left, at best.\""
  - line: 145
    type: narration
    text: "He met Geralt's eyes, then Oreck's. \"But this way... this way I matter.\""
  - line: 147
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck gripped his shoulder, the gesture speaking volumes."
  - line: 148
    type: narration
    text: "\"Die well, scout.\""
  - line: 150
    type: narration
    text: "Vek'tar managed a broken smile."
  - line: 151
    type: narration
    text: "\"I'll try not to die at all.\""
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "He didn't attack the Guardian's anchor points."
  - line: 154
    type: narration
    text: "Instead, he focused, chroniton energy crackling around him until his form became translucent, then insubstantial."
  - line: 155
    type: narration
    text: "With a final look at his companions, he phased—not at the Guardian, but directly into the radiant heart of the Shard of First Dawn."
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "The scream that followed wasn't sound."
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "It was light given voice—a silent, searing flash that blinded them all."
  - line: 160
    type: narration
    text: "When their vision cleared, the Guardian was stumbling, its connection to the Shard severed."
  - line: 161
    type: narration
    text: "The tendrils of corrupted light snapped and dissipated."
  - line: 163
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Now!\""
  - line: 164
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt roared."
  - line: 166
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck was already moving."
  - line: 167
    type: narration
    text: "His cleaver took the Guardian's head in a single, clean stroke."
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "The body collapsed, dissolving into motes of tarnished light that faded to nothing."
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "Silence returned to the chamber, broken only by their ragged breathing."
  - line: 172
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 4: THE EMPTY VICTORY"
  - line: 174
    type: narration
    text: "The Shard of First Dawn still floated at the chamber's center, but its light pulsed now with a strange, rhythmic cadence—like a heartbeat."
  - line: 176
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt approached cautiously."
  - line: 177
    type: narration
    text: "\"Vek'tar?\""
  - line: 179
    type: narration
    text: "No answer."
  - line: 180
    type: narration
    text: "The Shard was warm, alive, but silent."
  - line: 182
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Luminaire
    text: "\"His chroniton signature is... inside,\""
  - line: 184
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck stood beside Geralt, looking at the radiant crystal."
  - line: 185
    type: narration
    text: "\"Can we get him out?\""
  - line: 187
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I don't know. The Shard is ancient, pre-network. Its internal structure is beyond my understanding. But his consciousness is there. I can feel it.\""
  - line: 189
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt reached out, his armored fingers closing around the Shard."
  - line: 190
    type: narration
    text: "It was warm, almost comforting, but he felt no presence within it—just Light, pure and profound."
  - line: 192
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"We'll figure it out,\""
  - line: 194
    type: narration
    text: "They began the return journey, carrying the Shard of First Dawn."
  - line: 195
    type: narration
    text: "Carrying the hope that Vek'tar could be recovered, even as that hope grew fainter with each step."

